  "id": "asymptote",
  "term": "asymptote",
  "definition": "In item response theory, an asymptote is the limiting level that an item characteristic curve approaches. In the source context, the lower asymptote is the chance that very low-ability examinees still answer an item correctly, often because of guessing, partial knowledge, or ruling out wrong options.",
